        "id": "ch13_7_2-2",
        "text": "samba/smb.conf file and add the following line inside the [samba shares] directive:\nvalid users = @packt @alex\nBefore testing the new user\u2019s access to Samba, we will need to give the user alex access to the shared\ndirectory. To do this, we follow these steps:\n1.\nWe add the acl package in Ubuntu with the following command:\nsudo apt install acl\n2.\nThen we use the setfacl command to set read, write, and execute permissions for the /home/\npackt/samba_shares directory. For this, we use the following command:\nsudo setfacl -R -m \"u:alex:rwx\" /home/packt/samba_shares\nSetting up a Samba file server\n495\nIn the next section, we will show you how to access the Samba shares from different systems on\nthe network.",
